{#
  BeMart Help — 当サイトについて (EC-CUBE goHelpAbout).

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 default-theme `Help/about.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/default/Help/about.twig).

  Markup skeleton, `ec-role` / `ec-pageHeader` / `ec-off1Grid` /
  `ec-borderedDefs` / `ec-label` classes and the `<dl>`/`<dt>`/`<dd>`
  block structure are kept verbatim from EC-CUBE. The dynamic bindings
  are rebound to the Help/About resource body
  (src/Resource/Page/Help/About.php):
    staticContent.sections[] { id, label, value }

  EC-CUBE's `about.twig` reads each row off `BaseInfo` (shop_name,
  company_name, postal_code/pref/addr, phone_number, business_hour,
  good_traded, message), each wrapped in `{% if ... is not empty %}`.
  BeMart has no BaseInfo aggregation yet (Help/About is a Wave 3H pure
  renderer), so the resource body carries an EMPTY `staticContent.sections`
  list. With no sections the `{% for %}` emits no `<dl>` — exactly the
  empty `ec-borderedDefs` skeleton EC-CUBE renders when every BaseInfo
  field is empty. The populated rows are flagged as a MISSING BODY FIELD
  follow-up: a BaseInfo aggregation must surface shop/company/address
  facts into `staticContent.sections`. Enumerated as residual in
  tests/Resource/HelpAboutHtmlRenderTest.php.

  Each section's `<dd>` may carry newline-bearing prose (good_traded /
  message in EC-CUBE go through `|nl2br`); the port applies `|nl2br`
  uniformly so multi-line section values render the same.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md):
   - `{{ 'front.about.title'|trans }}` -> the ja literal "当サイトについて".
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% set route = 'help_about' %}
{% set title = '当サイトについて' %}

{% block main %}

<div class="ec-role">
    <div class="ec-pageHeader">
        <h1>当サイトについて</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="ec-off1Grid">
        <div class="ec-off1Grid__cell">
            <div class="ec-borderedDefs">
                {% for section in staticContent.sections %}
                    <dl id="help_about_box__{{ section.id }}">
                        <dt>
                            <label class="ec-label">{{ section.label }}</label>
                        </dt>
                        <dd>{{ section.value|nl2br }}</dd>
                    </dl>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
